<p>Thousands of people marched in Lyon, France, to pay tribute to 23-year-old far-right activist Quentin Deranque, who died in hospital last week from brain injuries. His death has sharpened political tensions and drawn national attention as investigators continue to piece together what happened.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/mBA8Y6HFc4gmDhd90JFejLGACUBDt0F4Ji7XBzIUj9_ItgjkCH7Vq5UcAFv-FkOT6rE0OjW3Ut_ztUBH_ec7Uh68k1y7nUWiJYWzw8eR_nd2xsZYary_Mrjmyk4SFG50ufUQh4NCRFuZMbkfEoACKYxT_xWR7DfAnYBmsMFxNYFRtOOX2AYADxut_Utvf6jhewoeCG5k_g' alt='A tribute march in Lyon following the death of far-right activist Quentin Deranque.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Security posture: Authorities kept the tribute march under heavy security, aiming to limit risks around the gathering.</li><li>National turnout: Euronews estimated more than 3,000 people marched across France in Deranque’s honour on Saturday.</li><li>Political fallout: The BBC said far-left militants are suspected in the killing, and the backlash has left Mélenchon’s party widely condemned as elections approach.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Emmanuel Macron: Macron called for calm ahead of the tribute march, urging restraint as tensions rose. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/hundreds-march-in-lyon-to-protest-far-right-activists-killing-as-macron-urges-calm/article70662353.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Lyon’s Green mayor: The city’s left-wing Green mayor asked the state to ban the rally, but officials allowed it to go ahead. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/thousands-march-in-lyon-after-french-far-right-activist-killed-last-week'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/hundreds-march-in-lyon-to-protest-far-right-activists-killing-as-macron-urges-calm/article70662353.ece'>Hundreds march in Lyon to protest far-right activist&#x27;s killing as Macron urges calm</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='http